# THE ACTUAL POST-CONDITION for policy mode KIOSK.
#
# apply-policy fails the build if any of these is still resolvable on the image after the removal
# pass, and kiosk/assert.sh checks the same list again inside the booted VM. Check S9 checks it a
# third time against the OCI image. Three independent checks of one list, because this is the single
# claim in the product that a customer can disprove by pressing a key.
#
# Binaries, not packages, because a package can be renamed and a binary cannot. If upstream moves
# plasmashell into a package called something else tomorrow, the removal fails loudly instead of
# shipping a kiosk with a desktop inside it.
#
# The three S9 names first. Everything after them is ours.
plasmashell
gnome-shell
sddm
gdm
lightdm
startplasma-wayland
startplasma-x11
plasma_session
konsole
xterm
gnome-terminal
dolphin
nautilus
plasma-discover
gnome-software
systemsettings
kinfocenter
